# Taiwan terminology & English finance terms

## Rule

In replies to the user and in any **UI / help text / notifications** you add or edit:

- Use **formal English** for standard valuation terms: WACC, FCFF, FCFE, CapEx, Terminal Value, SGR, Two-Stage DCF, Gordon model, MOS, etc.
- Use **Taiwan Traditional Chinese** for the rest (繁體、台灣用語).
- **Strictly avoid** Mainland Chinese, Hong Kong-only wording, and Simplified Chinese.

## Quick swap list

| Do not use | Use instead |
|------------|-------------|
| 默认 | 預設 |
| 参数 | 參數 |
| 数据 | 資料 |
| 用户 | 使用者 |
| 勾选 | 勾選 |
| 周期 | 週期 |
| 阈值 | 閾值 |
| 软件 | 軟體 |
| 网络 | 網路 |
| 信息 | 資訊 |
| 程序 / 代码 | 程式 / 程式碼 |
| 门限 | 閾值 |
| 质量 | 品質 |
| 账户 | 帳戶 |
| 报表 | 報表 |

## Valuation copy (theYNowApp)

- **永續成長率 g** / **終值 g** — not vague「成長率」 alone when meaning terminal.
- **暴衝平滑** / **暴衝倍數閾值** — CapEx spike rule; defaults (e.g. 1.35×, 3-year average) are **工程啟發式**, not academic standards; keep user-adjustable where exposed.
- Do **not** add ticker-specific formula branches; industry suggestions only via `industry_standards.R` / recommendation helpers.

